      "writtenOn": "2025-10-06T19:56:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t have a particularly strong opinion re: std::function vs Objective-C block, but if we make the change here, we should consider what to do about the ANGLE case. ANGLE can\u0027t return a std::function* cast to a void* and then cast back to a std::function* since that\u0027s technically undefined behavior, but it\u0027s defined behavior for an Objective-C block. We can make the change in Dawn native since the public API is C++ and compiled together with the calling code**, unlike ANGLE where it\u0027s a C API that\u0027s almost always dynamically linked (and is designed to allow compiling separately?).\n\nRe: returning the callable in EndAccess - that\u0027s a great idea - I\u0027ll look into the details.\n\n\n** Do we have any intention of making the Dawn native public interface be ABI safe? I.e. allow compiling with a different toolchain, compiler, flags, etc. and be dynamically linkable? Or is always meant to be compiled together with the calling code?",
